---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is robots txt guide in simple terms?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do I need to memorize all of this?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does it take to implement?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What happens if I get it wrong?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is this the same across all DNS providers?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Where can I get help if I'm stuck?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout title="robots.txt: The Complete Guide With Examples" description="robots.txt explained: syntax, user-agent groups, Disallow vs Allow, crawl-delay, sitemap directives, and the mistakes that deindex sites."  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ai-web-infrastructure/" class="hover:text-accent">AI Web Infrastructure</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">robots.txt Guide</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">robots.txt: The Complete Guide</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      robots.txt is the first file crawlers request on every site: a plain-text rulebook saying which
      user-agents may fetch which paths. It cannot force anything, but every major search and AI
      crawler respects it, which makes it the single highest-leverage file in technical SEO.
    </p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2>Anatomy</h2>
      <pre class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">User-agent: Googlebot
Disallow: /admin/
Allow: /admin/public/

User-agent: *
Disallow: /cart/
Disallow: /search

Sitemap: https://example.com/sitemap.xml</pre>
      <p>
        Rules group by user-agent: consecutive <code>User-agent</code> lines share the block that
        follows. <code>*</code> matches any bot without its own group. <code>Disallow</code> blocks a
        path prefix; an empty value disallows nothing. <code>Allow</code> carves exceptions inside
        disallowed trees. <code>Sitemap</code> lines can appear anywhere and should.
      </p>
      <h2>The rules behind the rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It lives at the root, exactly <code>/robots.txt</code>, one per host, served as text/plain.</li>
        <li>Most-specific group wins: a named bot ignores the wildcard group entirely.</li>
        <li>Path matching is prefix-based; <code>/blog</code> also blocks <code>/blogroll</code>. Use trailing slashes deliberately.</li>
        <li>Case matters for paths, not for directives.</li>
        <li>Some crawlers stop reading after 500 KB.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Mistakes that cost real traffic</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>Disallow: /</code> shipped from staging: the classic site-wide deindex.</li>
        <li>Blocking CSS/JS paths that pages need to render, degrading how search engines see the page.</li>
        <li>Expecting robots.txt to hide content: it only prevents crawling, not indexing of linked URLs; use noindex or auth for that.</li>
        <li>AI-era oversight: wildcard blocks written years ago now exclude GPTBot, ClaudeBot, and PerplexityBot too.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Check yours</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/robots-txt-checker/">robots.txt checker</a> validates syntax line by line and
        shows AI-bot verdicts; the <a href="/ai-crawler-checker/">AI crawler checker</a> goes deeper
        per bot.
      </p>
      
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is robots txt guide in simple terms?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need to memorize all of this?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does it take to implement?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens if I get it wrong?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is this the same across all DNS providers?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Where can I get help if I'm stuck?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover.</p></details></div>
<h2>Related</h2>
